996 0 obj
<<
/Title (The Location Quotient \(LQ\) is a ratio that is used to identify the significance of employment of an industry sector in a local economy compared to a larger reference economy.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 916 0 R
/Next 997 0 R
>>
endobj
997 0 obj
<<
/Title (An LQ below 1 indicates that an industry under represented in the local economy compared to the reference economy. An LQ of 1 suggests that the industry in both the local and reference economy are at equilibrium in their respective economies. When the LQ is greater than 1, it indicates that the industry more concentrated locally than the reference economy. Moreover, an LQ of greater than 1.25 typically indicates that the industry is an export-oriented based, contributing to economic growth that will further strengthen the local economy \(Leigh & Blakely, 2016\).)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 916 0 R
/Prev 996 0 R
>>
